18121:
Recall the formula for the mean free path of an ideal gas:
\lambda = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}\pi n d^2}
where n is the number density of the molecules and d is their molecular diameter.

Set up the ratio of mean free paths for gases A and B:
\frac{\lambda_A}{\lambda_B} = \frac{n_B d_B^2}{n_A d_A^2}
We are given:
\lambda_A = \frac{1}{2}\lambda_B \implies \frac{\lambda_A}{\lambda_B} = \frac{1}{2}
d_A = 2d_B

Substitute the given values and solve for n_A:
\frac{1}{2} = \frac{n_B d_B^2}{n_A (2d_B)^2} = \frac{n_B}{4n_A}
4n_A = 2n_B \implies n_A = \frac{1}{2}n_B

This matches Option (D).
→ (D)

18125:
Write the position and velocity equations of the particle:
s(t) = t^2 - 6t + 5
v(t) = \frac{ds}{dt} = 2t - 6

Identify the turning point:
Setting velocity to zero gives:
2t - 6 = 0 \implies t = 3\text{ s}
The particle reverses its direction of motion at t = 3\text{ s}.

Calculate the positions at key instants:
At t = 0\text{ s}: s(0) = 5\text{ m}
At t = 3\text{ s}: s(3) = 3^2 - 6(3) + 5 = 9 - 18 + 5 = -4\text{ m}
At t = 6\text{ s}: s(6) = 6^2 - 6(6) + 5 = 5\text{ m}

Determine the total distance travelled and average speed:
Distance from t = 0 to t = 3\text{ s}: |-4 - 5| = 9\text{ m}
Distance from t = 3 to t = 6\text{ s}: |5 - (-4)| = 9\text{ m}
Total distance: d = 9 + 9 = 18\text{ m}
Total time: \Delta t = 6\text{ s}
v_{\text{avg}} = \frac{\text{Total distance}}{\text{Total time}} = \frac{18\text{ m}}{6\text{ s}} = 3\text{ m s}^{-1}

This matches Option (C).
→ (C)

18126:
Calculate the mass defect (\Delta m) of the reaction:
Reaction: ^{238}\text{U} \rightarrow {}^{234}\text{Th} + {}^{4}\text{He}
Given masses:
Mass of reactants: m(^{238}\text{U}) = 238.050\text{ u}
Mass of products: m(^{234}\text{Th}) + m(^{4}\text{He}) = 234.043 + 4.003 = 238.046\text{ u}

\Delta m = 238.050 - 238.046 = 0.004\text{ u}

