\text{Co}^{3+} (3d^6). \text{NH}_3 acts as a strong field ligand with \text{Co}^{3+}:
t_{2g}^6 e_g^0 \implies n = 0 \text{ (diamagnetic, } \mu = 0\text{)}
(D) [\text{Ti(H}_2\text{O})_6]^{3+}:
\text{Ti}^{3+} (3d^1):
t_{2g}^1 e_g^0 \implies n = 1 \text{ unpaired electron}
\mu = \sqrt{3} \approx 1.73\text{ BM}

Compare magnetic moments:
[\text{Mn(CN)}_6]^{3-} has the maximum number of unpaired electrons (n = 2) and thus the highest spin-only magnetic moment (2.83\text{ BM}).

This corresponds to Option (A).
